{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341267-a-novate-in-chronicles-of-darkness","id":1341267,"title":"A novate in chronicles of darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-14T09:49:58-07:00","id":1341267,"title":"A novate in chronicles of darkness","content":"<b>Hello everyone.</b><br /> <br /> I am new to the page, I hope we get along.<br /> <br /> I am currently starting Vampire: The requiem with my friends, but honestly, I have read the book of chronicles of darkness and Vampire: Blood and Smocke and I would like to have recommendations, what kind of conflicts can I put on my friends, we come to play for 10 years in a row Dungeons and Dragons and for that game there is not much room for political problems, <b>THAT DON'T BE SOLVED FIGHTING</b>, vampire is a more obscure game of emotions, secrets and deceptions and to be honest I am not good at that type of conflict.<br /> Currently I have read <b>VERY</b> little about the hunters and I am studying how I could raise a conflict against hunters, to be able to put the emotion of the fight to the role and would like to have their advice, is it a good idea to put hunters? What kind of political conflicts do you like to use for your games? that another creature of the dark recommend me to not be a vampire to be able to use the fight in my game.<br /> <br /> <b>Thanks for your attention.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25701-lasombrax01","name":"LaSombrax01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T11:53:14-07:00","id":1341289,"title":"","content":"Welcome! Check out the links in my signature for links to a variety of books that might be helpful! <br /> <br /> First place I would start would with the Kindred\u2019s Touchstones. What types of stories can you tell that put them in danger without there being physical violence. Is a bank trying to seize their property? Are they in another Covenant\u2019s domain, who don\u2019t like you coming in to see them? Is there another supernatural parasite leeching away part of their life without killing them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T20:24:17-07:00","id":1341386,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m a big softy when it comes to politics as in I tend to build a safety net for my players when I come up with my city\u2019s court. On the subject of hunters remember that hunters exist because a vampire messed up, they are people who know something but nobody gave them a copy of the rule book and they won\u2019t just yell and attack. Play the hunters like you would run any of those DnD monsters that can change shape (succubus and doppelg\u00e4nger come to mind) and don\u2019t be afraid to let them make mistakes, if the hunters think someone is a vampire they should approach the situation accordingly and deal with the outcome as best they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T20:35:37-07:00","id":1341390,"title":"","content":"While not a VtR player, I can say that one of the big changes from DnD to CoD is that the former focuses on the triumphant use of force (magical or physical). CoD players can gain beats (and therefore experience) by accepting <i>failures</i> and complications that make the narrative more interesting, more dramatic. DnD tends to be <i>tactical</i> - you need to figure out which spells you should use to buff the fighters, and take out the traps or nuke the hordes. CoD has some of that, but there's a lot more <i>strategy:</i> who can you trust? Can you persuade your enemies to attack each other? How much of the safety of your friends are you willing to risk? How much of your self are you willing to sacrifice?<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> wrote, unlike many DnD games, the narrative flows not from what characters can <i>do</i>, but what they <i>value.</i> Is the respect of other vampires important to them? Has the Prince given them a task that serves as a complicated political trap? They're not questing for the amulet of Yendor, but instead trying drive off Hunters or save the life of their brother.<br /> <br /> In designing DnD adventures I tended to focus on maps and monsters. In designing a CoD game it was more about a web or network of actors, from street level to midlevel to major actors. In DnD it's dungeon levels, in CoD it's levels of response. Taking out a street gang will provoke a response from higher up the power structure, causing an attack from an unanticipated direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T13:22:15-07:00","id":1341502,"title":"","content":"Think: who is connected to whom and what is the nature of that connection? Who has more power in the connection? Is it formal or informal? What do they think of the other person?<br /> <br /> Now: your PCs and NPCs will constantly pull and shift these connections--sometimes by mere presence, as if with gravity. How does that change the behavior of others such that they fall out of stasis and into action? The nature of the connections pulled, and the predilections of the character involved, will determine which action is taken.<br /> <br /> Example: just because you're a newbie doesn't make you dog food among the more powerful. If they assume that you must be working for someone they will want to know who and what you are before taking action that would be otherwise reasonable and violent. That gives narrative breathing space to establish new characters as they slide through the uncertainty--the older, powerful entities are working to calibrate their sensors on the unknown blip... which gives the blip time to slide out of range or resolve into a &quot;safe&quot; state.<br /> <br /> I use the above principle to let otherwise squishy but mobile mortals interact with very dangerous vampires. They could easily be neonates (and in fact are sometimes mistaken as such). Characters do not walk around with a nametag on that declares everything.<br /> <br /> Well... except for those elysium events.<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24502\" data-vbnamecard=\"24502\">KieranMullen</a> wins an internet for the NetHack reference.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T08:42:19-07:00","id":1342085,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for your comments, they help me, I currently have a disaster at the Elysium, in fact it is now called Colosseum, because the person I put on is a Vampire bored of political affairs, however, it obviously has people submerged in those matters. This person is literally a puppet of something bigger (I still don't decide who or who), but I will probably make them face this one and if they are winners, that some of my players keep the position of prince.<br /> <br /> All your comments help me, anything you want to suggest with pleasure I will read and contemplate for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25701-lasombrax01","name":"LaSombrax01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T08:55:28-07:00","id":1342089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LaSombrax01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341267-a-novate-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1342085#post1342085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very much for your comments, they help me, I currently have a disaster at the Elysium, in fact it is now called Colosseum, because the person I put on is a Vampire bored of political affairs, however, it obviously has people submerged in those matters. This person is literally a puppet of something bigger (I still don't decide who or who), but I will probably make them face this one and if they are winners, that some of my players keep the position of prince.<br /> <br /> All your comments help me, anything you want to suggest with pleasure I will read and contemplate for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Roman Colosseum was created to be a grand venue for events that brought together the high and politically-connected with the lowly servant-class, so they could establish commonality in appreciating the blood-sport provided. The high would sponsor these (expensive) proceedings and would be appreciated for their generosity as well as a certain democracy in the results: &quot;fan favorites&quot; might receive mercy or rewards, so there was an illusion of largess as well. <br /> <br /> This is the &quot;circuses&quot; part of the phrase &quot;bread and circuses&quot;. It's purpose was to manage the factions in Rome and enable them to be ruled more easily. Everyone jostled within their class during these events, while also observing the protocols that placed them firmly <i>within</i> their class. They were a great distraction and are closely analogous to our modern sporting events--especially professional ones.<br /> <br /> The &quot;bread&quot; part of the phrase gets at feeding rights, and the parceling out of those right or resources such that everyone has something to eat. Those who are poor hunters are looked after, and those with larger areas may be asked to &quot;contribute&quot; to the ruler's provisions for the good of the community. <br /> <br /> A Prince who accomplishes both bread and circuses will be stable until the jaded tastes or stomachs of the populace grow beyond his or her means to support. At that point some greater... discipline--an example or few at least... will be needed to illustrate who is in charge. Maybe a foreign enemy to serve as a distraction?<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T16:37:20-07:00","id":1342221,"title":"","content":"The CofD core (the mortal one) book has a system for investigations if you want to spend the money on another book and feel that you need it. Don\u2019t be afraid to let Disciplines solve problems for you, a well made Mekhet is quite capable of handling most simple investigations for the group likewise mortals are not going to keep secrets from Dominate or Magisty.<br /> Equally important is that other vampires know this, if you have two Mekhet in the group and they don\u2019t spill the beans then is it unreasonable for an NPC to assume that they want paying off in some way?<br /> Their Sires might have solved the case but don\u2019t want to tell them what\u2019s going on because they should be able to solve it themselves or they might be safer not knowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T03:52:54-07:00","id":1343119,"title":"","content":"As both <b>CoD</b> and <b>D&amp;D</b>(-esque) Game Master, I advice you to start in <b>CoD</b> with <b>clear chronicle setup</b>. That means, focus on one, maybe two Factions/Covenants - and based story on that. It will be much more manageable and much clearer for you to focus games in particular atmosphere of the story. I will just break down to you basic 5 Covenants in <b>Requiem</b>:<ul><li><b>Carthian Movement </b>\u2013 revolution movies, like <i>Matrix</i> or <i>V for Vendetta</i></li> <li><b>Circle of the Crone </b>\u2013 pagan vampires worshiping \u2018Mother of Monsters\u2019 \u2013 movies like <i>Cult</i> or <a href=\"https://screenrant.com/midsommar-similar-folk-horror-films/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>many</i> pagan horrors</a>.</li> <li><b>Invictus </b>\u2013 modern/medieval political drama \u2013 stories like <i>Game of Thrones</i> ( without dragons, can work with \u2018zombies\u2019 / see Revenants in <b>Requiem</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> / ) or <i>House of Cards</i></li> <li><b>Lancea Sanctum</b> - Damned Church, stories like <i>Name of Roses</i>, <i>Interview with Vampire</i> ( much more movie ) or Inquisition.</li> <li><b>Ordo Dracul </b>\u2013 secrets societies, alchemy, legacy of <i>literal Dracula</i>. ( Movie adaptation are cool \u2013 also <b>Hellsing</b> and <b>Castlevania</b> anime series. ) Also, most crossover friendly with other monster races of CoD, if you want <i>later</i> add them. ( I do not advise crossovers from start \u2013 it\u2019s cool subgenere, but headache on the start. )</li> </ul>That are my two cents for new <b>CoD</b> / <b>Requiem</b> fellow Storyteller. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-23-2019, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T19:09:44-07:00","id":1343318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341267-a-novate-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1341502#post1341502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24502\" data-vbnamecard=\"24502\">KieranMullen</a> wins an internet for the NetHack reference.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I will keep it in an open field west of a white house, with a boarded front door. There is a small mailbox there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T09:38:37-07:00","id":1343444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1341267-a-novate-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1343318#post1343318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you! I will keep it in an open field west of a white house, with a boarded front door. There is a small mailbox there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At least it won't be dark. Except at night. <br /> <br /> [Had to google this one, sadly.]<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}